                <pb facs="0937" n="825" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg825"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 853.00/81.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Cage to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-10-05"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October 5,
                    1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>After fighting all night in the city and in front of legation where we have been
                    continuously since yesterday morning many Loyalist soldiers surrendered. Most
                    public buildings and some forts fly Republican flag. It is reported that the
                    King of Portugal is in Brazilian war vessel <hi rendition="#italic">S.
                        Paulo</hi> and that a republic has been proclaimed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gage.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
